A||||9||GREENDANO||85 GT vs. Big School Bus
Z||000000||GREENDANO||08-03-99||07:03 PM||||All right everybody, I was at the stop light yesterday just down the street from the school when a school bus pulled up next to me.  I looked over and he gave me the nod.  When the light turned green we took off.  It must have been one of the skunk-works busses because I could bearly see through all the tire smoke he left.  I then heard the turbo whistle, and I knew I was in trouble.  The bus put up a good fight and lead me for a while but I finally passed him when he slowed in the 20 MPH school zone and turned his flashing-safety lights on.  I knew the race was mine when I passed him as he was letting a kid off the bus to go to school.  I flipped him off through the open side door just to show him what a big man I was......<p>Doesn't this sound stupid??  Just a little joke and food for thought.  :)  <br>FLAME AWAY!!<br>  Dan-O
Z||000001||FieroWidow||08-03-99||07:18 PM||||Man, what a jerk!!  He does have a good point though.  I never was a fan of street racing and I think it's stupid and childish.<br> BTW, I have a GT and a Mustang 5.0.  NO WAY IN H*LL WILL A FIERO BEAT A MUSTANG!!!  We've raced them, switching drivers just to account for error.  The Ford tripped the timing lights first everytime.
Z||000002||Punkndrublic||08-03-99||11:53 PM||||A SCHOOL BUS???????? come man. You and me both know you can do better then that.<p>Its like this one time when i was driving in DOWNTOWN Vancouver right outside granville station. When i stopped at this intersection and a cop in one of those sup'd up camaros pulls up next to me and gets that ol push-rod 8 rumbling, so rev'd up overly cam'd out 6. Needless to say I felt a little insecure but he also weighs 1000 pounds more, the german shepard nawing on the drug dealer in the back didn't help him either. Anyways here i am thinking things couldn't get any worse when another cop, this time in one of those new mustang cobras they bought, pulls up on the otherside me. But get this its only a two lane intersection and the mustang is sitting in the left turn lane, but hell if the cop likes head-ons then thats what he ll get. Of course while this is all happening i m watching the other set of traffic lights so i get my timing right and leave right at the green. So it turns green and all i hear around me is the sound tires peeling out and the whole intersection fills up with smoke that smells like burning rubber. Of course i m such a pro and my rubbers are brand new none of the smoke was mine, my wheels chirp'd once, the engine got a dose of laughing gas, my boost gauge hit 40 psi and i was gone.<p>Haven't seen those cops around in long time, and for some reason the whole intersection been blocked of for construction. I wonder what happened????
Z||000003||Patrick||08-04-99||01:09 AM||||<br>I thought the full moon was a couple of nights ago... :)<p>
Z||000004||DJRice||08-04-99||07:08 AM||||I'll give this a try......<p>So Im stopped at a red light on the drive home from work yesterday, and I happen to shoot a glance out my back window and I see a blue streak in the sky.  After it did a double barrel roll, I could see that it was the #1 F-18 from the Navy's Blue Angels.  I continued to watch, because the light was still red, and he pulsed his afterburners.<br>Wondering if that was actually directed at me, I hit my headlight button and 'blinked' my lights.  He fired up his afterburners again and immeadiately shut them off.  As much as I hate to take a Navy jet to school, I knew what had to be done.  The light turned green and I dropped the hammer.  It was a close race until my automatic tranny dropped third gear ,which is when I went supersonic.<br>Even with his afterburners, he was not able to hang as the car shifted into 4th gear and I was travelling Mach 2+ (I know this because I had to upgrade my speedometer).  So after a few seconds of Mach 2 speeds, I backed off of the throttle to let him catch up with me.  I looked over to his cockpit and gave him a wave, he gave me the thumbs up.  <p>All I had left to do was find a break in traffic to land the car........Man, those performance lug nuts are amazing things.  I figure I gained about 1200HP.<p>NNEEXXTT......
Z||000005||RICK||08-04-99||07:30 AM||||I'm glad I have my boots on because it's getting DEEP in here!!
Z||000006||BN Boomer||08-04-99||08:43 AM||||That <b>story</b> is pretty funny, DJRice, especially when taking into consideration that the Blue Angels have been up here for the last few days practicing for their performance at the Seafair hydroplane races in Seattle, about as far away from Florida as you can get within the continental United States.<p>Hmmm...Hydroplanes, that reminds me of a race in my own Fiero a few years ago. You see, I was on the I-90 floating bridge across Lake Washington when all of sudden this hydroplane pulls up alongside me and the driver gives me the nod, so I gun my 87's 4 cylinder and the automaic tranny drops a gear just as I hear the Miss Bud's turbine engine spooling up to unbelievable RPMS. He had me by a pontoon length for about the first 93 inches, but then I managed to start steadily pulling away from him. I had a good 9/16s car length on him when he finally had to back off and give up as the shore loomed closer and he ran out of water.<p>Next week, fond recollections of the time I whipped a diesel Chevette.
Z||000007||kel||08-04-99||01:48 PM||||Sometimes when you just want a laugh, that's all you have to do is go to the Fiero Forum and read.......... :)
Z||000008||Patrick||08-04-99||03:53 PM||||<br>Hey Boomer, I hear the Chevette actually had you, but it had to slow down because the boat and trailer was geting too snakey behind it!:)<p>Speaking about Miss Bud, I really did have a chance to race her last Saturday. She was sitting on her trailer parked on the side of a street here in Vancouver. Even when she's standing still, she looks a whole lot faster than my Fiero does at full throttle with a tail wind.<p>
Z||000009||batboy||08-04-99||06:44 PM||||Some funny stories, but I still like my  "Raced a Lamborghini Diablo" tale in another thread (last updated 6-22-99 I think).
